ZYROX is a rebranded distribution of the ollama-termux installer and ships
the pre-built ollama-termux Android ARM64 runtime binaries. It preserves the
upstream MIT license and attribution chain.

Upstream projects:
- ollama-termux (Termux-first Android ARM64 fork of Ollama, MIT):
  https://github.com/DioNanos/ollama-termux
  Copyright 2026 Davide A. Guglielmi
- Ollama (MIT): https://github.com/ollama/ollama — Copyright Ollama
- llama.cpp (MIT): https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

The runtime downloaded and installed by ZYROX (ollama, llama-server and ggml
backend libraries) is built and published by the upstream ollama-termux
project. ZYROX verifies every download with SHA256 before installing.

Gemini cloud chat uses the Google Generative Language API
(generativelanguage.googleapis.com) with the user's own API key.
